# Pin LF on codegen-sensitive artifacts so cross-platform checkouts read
# byte-identical content. Without this, Git's autocrlf=true on Windows
# would store CRLF and a Linux contributor's checkout would fail
# `npm run codegen:verify` because their LF-generated output would not
# byte-match the CRLF-converted committed file.
#
# Scope is intentionally narrow — do NOT broaden to the whole repo.
scripts/openapi-snapshot.json text eol=lf
src/shared/api-types.ts text eol=lf

# Same rationale for the vendored 022 design handoff: these files are committed
# VERBATIM and RECONCILIATION.md asserts they are byte-identical to the
# designer's bundle. Without a pin, autocrlf=true would materialise CRLF on a
# Windows checkout and that verbatim claim would hold only on some platforms.
# Binary assets (PNG) are unaffected. Scope stays narrow — this directory only.
specs/022-pos-ui-v4-rescue/design-handoff/**/*.html text eol=lf
specs/022-pos-ui-v4-rescue/design-handoff/*.css text eol=lf
specs/022-pos-ui-v4-rescue/design-handoff/*.md text eol=lf
